    {
      "id": "root-tutorial-poster-try",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Try it",
      "position": {
        "x": 2130,
        "y": -200
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "Try it",
        "body": "1. Find the card on the stage. It is this graph’s own root: the node the graph begins from. A file has exactly one.\n2. Switch to edit mode (the pencil). Hover over the card and press Edit, at its top right. The card grows into an editor, and goes back to its own size when you press Done.\n3. Change the name. Everything that lists this graph shows the new name; it lives here and nowhere else.\n4. Clear the name. The field turns red, and says a graph needs a name before it can be saved. The version, the description and the kind are the same.\n5. Look at Surfaces, at the bottom. Each is a chain of faces that ends in a Glyph. They are drawn on the canvas, not typed here.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "root-tutorial-poster"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
